# From "NVC II" (Wave IV - Adventure, CD3-5) -- continues nvc-i.gws with
# living things in motion, then abstract concepts, then the settled Gateway
# Affirmation itself, translated nonverbally line by line. Same condensing
# approach as nvc-i.gws: a representative selection in the source's order,
# ASR noise dropped.

@segment  nvc-ii
@title    NVC II — Nonverbal Communication
@levels   F12
@duration ~5m

say Your next exercise in nonverbal communication. Same as before — picture each thing the moment you hear it, release it the moment the next one comes.
pause 6
say A soaring bird.
pause 3
say A running dog.
pause 3
say A climbing monkey.
pause 3
say A trotting horse.
pause 3
say A hopping rabbit.
pause 3
say A swimming fish.
pause 3
say A walking man.
pause 3
say Relax.
pause 5
say Now feelings and concepts, the same way.
pause 5
say Need.
pause 3
say Want.
pause 3
say Eager.
pause 3
say Curious.
pause 3
say Question.
pause 3
say Understand.
pause 3
say Accept.
pause 3
say Reject.
pause 3
say Help.
pause 3
say Hello.
pause 3
say Compassion.
pause 3
say Yes.
pause 3
say No.
pause 3
say Relax.
pause 6
say Now restate your affirmation, nonverbally, one line at a time.
pause 6
say I am more than my physical body.
pause 5
say Because I am more than physical matter.
pause 5
say I can perceive that which is greater than the physical world.
pause 5
say Therefore, in these exercises, I deeply desire to expand.
pause 5
say To experience.
pause 4
say To know.
pause 4
say To understand.
pause 4
say To control.
pause 4
say To use such greater energies and energy systems as may be beneficial and constructive to me, and to those who follow me.
pause 6
say Also, I deeply desire the help and cooperation, the understanding, of those whose wisdom, development, and experience are equal or greater than my own.
pause 6
say I ask their guidance and protection from any influence or source that might provide me with less than my stated desires.
pause 6
say Relax.
pause 5
say Move now to Focus 12 by the nonverbal method you've learned. Focus 12.
pause 5
say Use your expanded awareness to perceive whatever nonverbal information is available. I'll call you when it's time to return.
pause 6
hold 60
say You'll remember it in full, and be able to put it into words once you're back.
pause 6
say Move now back to Focus 10.
pause 5
